          "type": "TextualBody",
          "label": "Verso (fourth section of join): T-S AS 74.141r + T-S NS 329.820v",
          "value": "\n<ol><li>They said to him: &ldquo;And why&nbsp; did you deal with these things,&nbsp;</li>\n<li>and you teach an evil teaching to all creatures?</li>\n<li>And these books that are in your hand&mdash;if you tell&nbsp;</li>\n<li>us the truth, whose (books) they are; and if not, we will kill</li>\n<li>you, and t[hro]w your body to the animals of the field.&rdquo;</li>\n<li>He said to them: &ldquo;These writings are not old</li>\n<li>and they are not new, and they are not by Balaam.&rdquo;</li>\n<li>They said to him: &ldquo;And from where do you have them?&rdquo; He said: &ldquo;They are by Yoh\u0323anan</li>\n<li>the Dyer, and he is my teacher, and he gave them to me</li>\n<li>and I learned them.&rdquo;&nbsp; Pilatus the governor answered</li>\n<li>and said to Marinus the elder of the Jews:</li>\n<li>&ldquo;Where is this Yoh\u0323anan the Dyer?&rdquo; He said</li>\n<li>him: &ldquo;In [the town of ?] Kephar [Nah\u0323um]. And if [... ...]&rdquo;</li></ol>\n",
          "format": "text/html"
        }
      ],
